<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso XI of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1311">1311</a>–<a href="/years/1350">1350</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso XI was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León from 1312 to 1350. After a long minority he restored royal authority, and in 1340, with Afonso IV of Portugal, he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rio-salado">Battle of Río Salado</a>. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a> in 1344 and gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siete-partidas">Siete Partidas</a> force of law in 1348, but died of plague while besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-xi-of-castile.jpg" alt="Alfonso XI of Castile" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown source · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Libro_de_la_Coronaci%C3%B3n_de_los_Reyes_de_Castilla--2_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
